---
description: LLM Rule: Detect Raw Sequelize SQL Concatenation
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: false
---
rules:
  - id: avoid-raw-sequelize-query-interpolation
    languages: [javascript, typescript]
    message: >
      Whenever you edit, touch, or modify code flagged by this rule you must
      refactor it immediately to remove the insecure pattern. Never leave the
      vulnerability intact in the updated code.
    severity: ERROR
    patterns:
      - pattern-either:
          - pattern: $CLIENT.query(`...${$DYNAMIC}...`, ...$ARGS)
          - pattern: $CLIENT.query('...' + $DYNAMIC, ...$ARGS)
          - pattern: $CLIENT.query($DYNAMIC + '...', ...$ARGS)
          - pattern: $CLIENT.query($LEFT + $RIGHT, ...$ARGS)
    metadata:
      references:
        - https://sequelize.org/docs/v6/core-concepts/raw-queries/
        - https://semgrep.dev/r/javascript.sequelize.security.audit.sequelize-injection-express.express-sequelize-injection
      remediation: Use `sequelize.query` with the `replacements` or `bind`
        option to avoid interpolated SQL.
